        "original_id": "ca3f1cb5-85ae-5a68-a714-f2abdc564047",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles Hutchison, William K. Howard, Alma Hanlon, Florence Short, Mary Doyle\n- Films: The Golden God, The Thundering Herd, The Power and the Glory, Fire Over England, Johnny Come Lately\n- Roles: actor, director\n\nFacts:\n- Charles Hutchison appeared in 49 films between 1914 and 1944.\n- Charles Hutchison directed 33 films between 1915 and 1938.\n- The 1917 film The Golden God stars Charles Hutchison, Alma Hanlon, Florence Short, and Mary Doyle.\n- William K. Howard directed over 50 films from 1921 to 1946.\n- William K. Howard was considered one of Hollywood's leading directors.\n- William K. Howard's films include The Thundering Herd (1925), The Power and the Glory (1933), Fire Over England (1937), and Johnny Come Lately (1943).",
